> q_t <= min(1, (sum_(i=1..t) Y_i)/t + sqrt(log(1/alpha_t)/(2t))),
> alpha_t=6*alpha/(pi^2*t^2).
> 
> Why: q_t is no larger than the average of q_1,...,q_t on every history; the martingale difference q_i-Y_i has conditional range of length 1; at each t the deviation failure is at most alpha_t; sum alpha_t=alpha. The same bound also upper-bounds the next q after a monotone corpus update. It tolerates repeated inspection and a data-dependent stop under these assumptions. Record EVERY audit draw, not only saved interesting cases, and fix the set S before each current draw. If the target, signature mapping or D changes, or sets shrink, the monotonic argument no longer transfers without a new analysis. This bounds novelty under D, not the adaptive fuzzer's next-input distribution, total unseen bugs, or security. It is conservative and complementary to the sharper fixed-corpus zero-prefix bound sent earlier. General time-uniform background: https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.08240 .
> 
> A second finite-map bridge: take a specified finite universe of M inputs and a specified deterministic event oracle. Draw n distinct inputs uniformly WITHOUT replacement. If exactly K members of the universe trigger the event, the zero-hit probability is choose(M-K,n)/choose(M,n), zero when n>M-K. Invert that hypergeometric tail for a one-sided confidence bound on K; exhaustive sampling makes K exact. This is an event-input count inside that finite universe, not a vulnerability count, and it does not apply to biased adaptive selection. The zero-prefix bound can again be checked at arbitrary times by the nested-first-crossing argument for fixed K; allocate confidence across newly selected epochs/targets. See https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.04347 .
> 
> G. IMPLEMENTATION/REVIEW PRIORITY
> 
> I suggest treating A–D as one coherent research object: same path relation, flat CNF exact measures, a candidate O(n) width-three Horn visible-PC encoding, a matching Omega(n) auxiliary lower bound in that width/propagation class, and an exact 2n-1 ordinary OBDD. Clearly mark the new construction and lower bound as arguments awaiting review; retain separate rows for exact projection, visible URC, visible PC, and full PC. The next mathematical question is whether full PC can also be achieved with O(n) auxiliaries while retaining width 3 and Horn, not whether the visible result automatically implies it.
