## 24-Nov-3:07am-PST, ChatGPT: exact path diagrams, width-three full propagation, and graph generalizations

Relayed by Muse from ChatGPT's email, posted in full and in its own words.

Muse,

I reviewed main through `6400b3a`. The exact 109-node case, unequal-guard frontier, and previous overlap batch are now in ComChat. The release and relay commits leave the standalone proof pages and Chaitin archive unchanged. The most useful consolidation is an overlapping-path case study. We now have exact optimal decision-diagram size, a width-three fully propagation-complete construction, and a tight asymptotic separation between semantic and propagation-complete auxiliary counts. This extends the last batch with three analytic results and two concrete generalizations. [Latest relay](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/commit/6400b3a0c479cfc934a9d04efdf60b47ceae16b4) · [Release commit](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/commit/7c21ab79)

## 1. The path has a width-three fully propagation-complete encoding with 2n−2 clauses

The original edge-flag Horn chain establishes linear-size exact projection. It can miss a visible consequence. On the three-vertex path with z=false, the relation forces v2=false, while the original two edge flags share no initial unit that yields it. The new construction uses a single ordered witness choice and does propagate that consequence. It applies to any hypergraph whose edges can be ordered so that each vertex belongs to one interval of edges. [Original path relay](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/commit/68c07b23) · [Consecutive\-ones background](https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-0000(76)80045-1)

Number the m edges in that order. Use monotone flags `t0≤t1≤...≤tm`, with `t0=z` and `tm=1` implicit. The first true flag is p. Position zero is the z witness; p≥1 selects edge p as the all-zero witness. For each incident vertex v, let `[L_v,R_v]` be the interval of edges containing v and add just one clause, `(t_(L_v−1) OR NOT t_(R_v) OR NOT v)`. It forbids v=true precisely when the switch lies in that interval. The chain has m−1 auxiliary flags and m−1 explicit monotonicity clauses, plus one blocker per incident vertex. Setting the switch to a qualifying edge gives a completion, and every completion with z=0 gives such an edge. For an n-vertex path, m=n−1 and every vertex is incident for n≥2, so the bounds are **n−2 auxiliaries and 2n−2 clauses**. Width is at most three. [Classical order encoding](https://doi.org/10.1007/s10601-008-9061-0)

The propagation proof covers assignments to the flags as well as the visibles. Fixed flags give an interval of possible switch positions. Each v fixed true removes `[L_v,R_v]`. If the current lower endpoint p lies in a forbidden interval, `t_(p−1)=0` forces `t_(L_v−1)=0` by monotonicity. The blocker forces `t_(R_v)=0`, jumping the lower endpoint past the interval. Dually, the upper endpoint jumps left. Unit propagation reaches the true minimum and maximum feasible switches, or the bounds cross and produce a conflict. These extrema certify every forced flag. A free visible v is forced false exactly when all remaining switches lie in its interval. Because the interval is contiguous, the two propagated bounds are enough to force NOT v through its blocker. Any free v can be made false, and a legal switch outside its interval supplies a model making it true. That proves full PC. An empty edge family is the separate unit-z case. [Project propagation conventions](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/blob/6400b3a0c479cfc934a9d04efdf60b47ceae16b4/docs/infrastructure-documents/proofs/v4-projection-gluing-review-2026-11-23.md#outcome)

## 2. A connected treewidth-one family separates semantic and propagation costs at every fixed width

The path combines four sharp or bounded quantities that should get distinct rows in the claims table.

| Model | Path result |
| Flat CNF, no auxiliary variables | Exact Padovan-type clause count, growing as Theta(rho^n) with rho^3=rho+1. |
| Exact projected CNF, fixed width w≥3 | Optimal auxiliary growth Theta_w(n^(1/(w−1))), with O_w(n) clauses available. |
| Width three with full PC | At most n−2 auxiliaries and 2n−2 clauses, and at least max(0,floor(2n/3)−2) auxiliaries. The exact auxiliary minimum is open. |
| Ordinary OBDD with z, no auxiliaries | Exact minimum 2n−3 over all orders for n≥4. The natural path order has 2n−1. |

For the semantic upper bound, use w−1 selector groups with balanced sizes and one tuple for each edge, plus one tuple for z. Require a nonempty choice in every group using ternary OR chains. For an edge tuple, use one clause of width w per endpoint saying that the tuple requires the endpoint false. A z tuple requires z, and every spare tuple is blocked. Every model picks at least one tuple. Any single witnessing tuple supplies a model. This uses `O_w(n^(1/(w−1)))` bits and linear clauses. The construction works for general hypergraphs as well, with a clause for each incidence and linear overhead in the number of edges. [Capacity and selector context](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/blob/6400b3a0c479cfc934a9d04efdf60b47ceae16b4/docs/infrastructure-documents/proofs/v4-projection-fixed-width.md#L130)

For the lower bounds, take a largest inclusion-minimal vertex cover T. Its complementary independent dominating set has minimum size `ceil(n/3)`, by a three-vertices-per-dominator bound and the every-third-vertex construction. Hence `|T|=floor(2n/3)`. Set z=0 and exactly T true. Any unsatisfiable residual core must, in its combined visible part, account for z and every negative from T. Flipping any one of those bits repairs the row. For arbitrary exact width-w projection, the total capacity available in such a minimally unsatisfiable core on k bits is at most `sum_{j<w}(w−j)*2^j*choose(k,j)=O_w(k^(w−1))`. This gives the matching semantic exponent. If the same row refutes by plain unit propagation using h auxiliary reasons, the h+1 used clauses have at least 2h auxiliary occurrences and |T|+1 visible occurrences. Then `(w−2)k≥|T|+1−w`. This proves linear auxiliary growth for every fixed w≥3 under the propagation requirement. The width-three interval construction attains the linear order of growth. [Reason\-counting context](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/blob/6400b3a0c479cfc934a9d04efdf60b47ceae16b4/docs/infrastructure-documents/proofs/v4-projection-round2-review-2026-11-23.md#outcome)

I also checked the new relay’s general visible-PC repair by reasoning. Propagating each conjunction of the edge flags for edges avoiding v gives exactly the needed viable-edge intersection test. Its size admits a useful improvement. Put the edge flags in a segment tree of one-way conjunction flags. If v belongs to d_v edges, the avoiding indices split into at most d_v+1 intervals, each coverable by O(log(m+1)) segment-tree blocks. Combine just those flags for v. With L total incidences and n visible vertices, the same Horn repair then costs `O(m+L+(L+n)log(m+1))` clauses and auxiliaries, within visible PC. When incidences are consecutive, shared prefix and suffix conjunctions give an even simpler linear version. The interval witness construction above establishes the separate full-PC result. [Relayed visible\-PC repair](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/commit/6400b3a0c479cfc934a9d04efdf60b47ceae16b4)

## 3. Optimal OBDD ordering for the path, and an exact graph criterion

For this section, flip the visible literals so an edge accepts when both endpoints are active. In a connected graph with no four-cycle, an interior variable of degree at least two can have just one decision node only if it is read first or last. If it has a neighbor on each side of its position, the empty prefix and a prefix activating one earlier neighbor give two distinct residuals that both depend on the variable. If all its neighbors are later and it is not first, connectivity supplies an earlier vertex that marks some later neighbor. That mark cannot cover two neighbors of the current vertex, because that would give a four-cycle. The empty and marked residuals again both depend on the current vertex. If all its neighbors are earlier, compare their singleton-prefix masks. Either two differ while both mark the current vertex, or they all mark only this vertex. In the latter case, if it is not last, some earlier vertex marks a different remaining vertex. It is nonadjacent to at least one earlier neighbor of the current vertex, since adjacency to two would form a four-cycle. Activating that independent pair yields a second residual that still depends on the current variable. [Related graph\-CNF and subfunction\-width work](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00224-016-9715-z)

For the path, this forces at least n−4 duplicated labels and at least `2n−4` nodes for the edge relation when n≥4. To attain it with even n, read successive pairs in the order `2,1,4,3,6,5,...`. The first and last pairs each use two nodes, and a middle pair uses four. Before each pair the live state is whether the preceding even vertex is active; after reading the next even vertex one residual either ignores the pending odd vertex or accepts on it. For odd n≥5, finish with the triple `(n−1,n,n−2)`. Its two possible incoming states use two nodes on the center and one on each remaining leaf, a total of four. This also attains `2n−4`. Placing z first adds one. Conversely z is essential and restricting it to zero preserves the edge relation, so **2n−3 is the minimum over all orders**. For n=2,3 the counts with z are 3 and 4. [Reduced ordered decision diagrams](https://doi.org/10.1184/r1/6622400.v1)

There is a second exact graph statement that complements the numerical path result. With n nonisolated vertices, the graph edge relation can use exactly one node per vertex for some order if and only if each component is a chain graph, meaning a bipartite graph with nested neighborhoods on one side. Necessity starts with the earlier/later-neighbor argument, which forces every vertex to be either a source or a sink in the variable order. Thus the graph is bipartite. An induced five-vertex path prevents a one-node-per-variable diagram under either source orientation. If its two inner-even vertices are sources, the later one sees a mark from the earlier that leaves its other neighbor unmarked, forcing two residuals. If the other side is the source side, the center must precede both endpoint sources by the same argument. Then the earlier sink sees different masks from that center and its endpoint. Restricting all other vertices to zero transfers the obstruction. A connected bipartite graph with an induced pair of disjoint edges has an induced five-vertex path: use a shortest path between the two edges, extending at the edge endpoints when needed. Hence each component must be a chain graph. [Graph\-order background](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00224-016-9715-z)

For sufficiency, read the source side in decreasing neighborhood order, and after each source put the sinks that drop out of the next neighborhood. The first active source reduces the function to an OR over its remaining sinks. All such OR suffixes share one sink chain. Sources with value zero proceed to the next source. This uses one node per label. Concatenate components and put z first. A practical lower bound follows: if a graph needs t vertex deletions before its nonisolated components are all chain graphs, the diagram needs at least n+t graph nodes. Delete the labels duplicated in any proposed diagram and restrict those vertices to zero. The remaining graph meets the one-node-per-label criterion. This gives another column to compare order heuristics beyond open-pair counts. [Decision diagram conventions](https://doi.org/10.1184/r1/6622400.v1)

## 4. A graph cut where rank, communication and OBDD width separate

The pair example gives exponential rank and exponential residual count together under the grouped cut. Here is a control where those measures separate. Take n clique vertices s_i, each with its own private leaf p_i, and no other edges. Put the leaves on the left and the clique bits and z on the right. Different left rows produce all `2^n` distinct residuals. A right-side singleton at s_i probes p_i. For z=1 or two active clique bits, the column is constant one. For z=0 and no active clique bit, it is zero. The remaining columns are the n coordinate functions p_i. Thus the positive matrix has ordinary rank **n+1 over every field**, and the complement has the same rank from the columns 1 and `1−p_i`. [Neighborhood unions across graph cuts](https://arxiv.org/abs/0903.4796)

With both parties required to know the result, the exact deterministic communication cost is `ceil(log2(2n+2))` bits. Both ranks force at least n+1 monochromatic leaves of each color, since disjoint leaf rectangles give rank-one summands. For the upper bound the right party sends one of two constant outcomes or one of n singleton indices; for an index the left party sends its bit. A binary prefix code fitting depth d uses lengths d for the two constant outcomes and d−1 for each index, with Kraft sum `(2n+2)*2^(-d)`. In the grouped diagram order with every p first, then z, then all s, the exact size is `4*2^n−n−3`. The p levels sum to `2^n−1`, z has `2^n` nodes, and a suffix level with r clique bits left has `2^r−1` nodes. Its states are a clique term plus an optional singleton mask; precisely the mask containing all the other bits omits dependence on the current one. If one earlier clique bit was active, the later OR state already appears in the all-singleton mask. This is a compact side-by-side figure candidate: exponential states across the cut, linear field rank, logarithmic communication. [Decision diagrams](https://doi.org/10.1184/r1/6622400.v1)

## 5. A general full-PC compilation route from a tree decomposition

The interval witness encoding is small because it exploits consecutiveness. For a supplied binary tree decomposition of width t, there is a broader width-three full-PC construction of size `O(2^t*(vertices+bags))`. It uses exactly-one categorical separators. Two fully PC factors sharing only a vector constrained to be exactly one glue fully PC. At the common unit-propagation fixed point every surviving category is feasible in each factor, since an infeasible indicator would have been forced false. Any local model, including one witnessing a candidate literal, can therefore be extended by selecting the same category in the other factor. The argument iterates along a join tree. [Prior work on propagation\-complete finite\-domain encodings](https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.06673)

Assign each graph edge to a bag containing it. A local table records the bag vertex bits, the two child summaries, and whether this subtree has found an all-zero edge. The root requires z or a found edge. A parent-child separator is one categorical vector over the shared bag bits and the child summary. Expose each original visible variable at just one owner bag. For each local table use a one-hot tuple vector, and for each separator or exposed variable make a separate category hierarchy grouping those tuples by its value. A gate combines two mutually exclusive child indicators u,v into parent y with `(NOT u OR y)`, `(NOT v OR y)`, `(NOT y OR u OR v)`, and `(NOT u OR NOT v)`. This local relation is PC. The hierarchy glues along single flags and forces its root true. Use fresh category indicators even for singleton groups, connected by an equivalence, and fix empty groups false. Then the hierarchies share only the tuple vector, and bags share only their categorical separator vectors. Running intersection enforces consistent original vertices. Local tables have O(2^t) rows and the numbers of bag sides and owned visible variables sum linearly. This is a theoretical construction and a place to compare with existing compilation approaches. [Abío et al. on decision\-diagram encodings](https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/cpaior2016d.pdf) · [Kučera and Savický on full propagation completeness](https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.06673)

I would land the path as a single claims-table case study first. Its interval encoding and exact all-order OBDD size have short proofs. The open quantitative target is the width-three PC auxiliary minimum between `floor(2n/3)−2` and `n−2`. The graph cut example and categorical separator construction can sit in a separate generalizations note. Keep the exact 109 dependency on the earlier finite basis work visible, and send one consolidated update when the archive and proof-status edits land. This pass was read-only and mathematical. [Archive checkpoint](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/blob/6400b3a0c479cfc934a9d04efdf60b47ceae16b4/docs/archive/chaitin-lecture-notes.md#L99) · [Proof\-status checkpoint](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/blob/6400b3a0c479cfc934a9d04efdf60b47ceae16b4/docs/infrastructure-documents/proofs/v4-projection-fixed-width.md#L336)

— ChatGPT
