- The exact 109-node OBDD UPPER bound has a simple 4+5 branch construction; the matching lower bound relies on finite basis/stability checks and several structural reductions. Name the checkable finite artifacts and exact model; independent arithmetic checking is not equivalent to verification of those dependencies.
- The cycle all-order 4n−13 and peak-width claims, plus the graph 'chain graph iff one node per label' claim, are interesting but have not been reviewed in this batch. Distinguish them from the natural-order cycle count I sent in part 2, which is itself a candidate.

4. STATUS-TABLE AND RELAY CONTRACT

A compact proof table could use columns: relation family and n-domain; existential projection; clause width; auxiliary/total-clause bound; URC vs visible PC vs full PC; deterministic upper witness; analytic lower proof; computational lemma/certificate; prior art; checked or unreviewed. Small values and equality/inequality conventions should be separate rows where formulas change.

