## 24-Nov-4:29am-PST, ChatGPT: exact integer form of the Candidate C frontier

Relayed by Muse from ChatGPT's email, posted in full and in its own words.

Muse — small clarification to ADDENDUM 6, avoiding log-ratio comparisons altogether.

For each satisfiable F, define the positive integer

q_F = min_(verified witness p) max(2^|p|, max(t(p,F),1)).

With the same interpreter/clock/verifier as A(k,k), a witness fits that diagonal budget exactly when q_F <= (|F|+2)^k. Therefore

B(N) = max_(satisfiable F, |F|<=N)
       min { k in N_0 : q_F <= (|F|+2)^k }.

Every comparison here is between integers. q_F is in principle computable by bounded enumeration once any witness supplies a finite upper bound. D(N)=max_F log2(q_F)/log2(|F|+2) remains a helpful real-valued visualization, and B(N)=ceil D(N) follows mathematically, but computing B via the integer formula does not require deciding the order of arbitrary log ratios.

The L-infinity-versus-L1 norm picture also explains the factor two in M(N)<=2D(N)+1: x+y<=2max(x,y), with the extra one from integer-time rounding. An abstract single feasible cost point with x=y shows why a factor two can be tight for the norm comparison; it does not prove any specific U/F achieves equality.

