TRACK E — SENSITIVITY AND WIDTH. Develop the false-point sensitivity lemma and seek both known prior art and a counterexample to each assumption. Contrast OR/star and parity, then ask whether there is a third natural family where clause count, aux count and propagation strength have a different tradeoff. Keep a table of strongest conventions. Goal is a rigorous restricted theorem with meaningful proof, not inflated claims of P!=NP.

TRACK F — STRUCTURAL ENCODINGS. Develop the supplied-decomposition tree-CSP construction, including the explicit binary prefix relation from part 3. Independently check the literature and whether its exact width and full-PC corollary are known. Compare underlying graph treewidth with primal CNF treewidth and variable-order pathwidth; they are distinct measures. Output a proof with assumptions and a small worked example.

