B. Independently verify all quantifiers, especially fixed k vs growing k and program output formatting.
C. Build a tiny illustration if spare capacity is real, but mark it a finite toy, not SAT hardness.
D. Try to overcome BOTH obstacles for a proposed diagonal construction: the formula changes the program range, and every valid witness must be excluded.

For context, Korten–Santhanam study conditional deterministic constructions of time-bounded random strings, while Huang–Li–Zhong study circuit range avoidance; their assumptions and problems are different from this input-dependent all-SAT-witness condition.
