The previous part has a real limit. This part supplies an equally concrete way around it for one algebraic class. Put the two examples together before proposing that the author commit to a single exact state representation.

For a satisfiable affine Boolean system over F_2, split columns at a cut and write

    A_P p + A_S s = b.

Each distinct nonempty reachable exact suffix residual is a fiber of s↦A_S s. The possible syndromes are the intersection (b+im A_P)∩im A_S, an affine coset of im A_P∩im A_S. Let λ=rank(A_P)+rank(A_S)−rank(A). Then exactly 2^λ fibers are reached. They are pairwise disjoint and nonempty. Exact semantic dominance among individual reachable nonempty residuals therefore cannot discard one and still preserve their union. This sharpens the limit of the explicit frontier even if the merge test could decide implication for free.

An exact compact projection still exists. Maintain a basis of im A_P as columns move from suffix to prefix. Take the rows of Q to span the left annihilator of im A_P. The existential projection on the suffix is

    Q A_S s = Q b.

For any satisfying suffix, solve the linear system A_P p=b−A_S s to lift it. Basis updates, annihilator and lifting cost polynomial time. In particular this gives a constructive algebraic operator for a known affine system represented as local parity CNF, or for CNF accompanied by the verified system. A recognition or conversion step must be charged if the input CNF is arbitrary.

A useful hybrid already has a completely charged algorithm. Given an affine system plus k ordinary CNF clauses, apply inclusion–exclusion on the k clause-falsification events. A subset of falsified clauses imposes unit linear equations, one per literal, and Gaussian elimination counts that intersection as zero or 2^(n−rank). Summing those 2^k terms gives exact counting in 2^k·poly(input), with witness reconstruction by prefix fixing and repeated counts. For k=O(log input) this is polynomial even when listing affine residuals is exponential. Finding such a decomposition from arbitrary CNF is a separate problem.

Bounded-degree expander Tseitin CNFs give a substantive example. With even total charge they are satisfiable and they have established exponential read-once branching-program lower bounds, hence exponential OBDD size in every order. The exponential OBDD bound implies some cut has exponentially many live residuals, since total nodes are at most the sum of live counts across levels. At such a cut the disjoint fibers make the explicit existential antichain exponentially large, while the affine summary and lift remain polynomial. Three separate quantities can thus diverge on one declared family: exact deterministic OBDD size, an explicit list of non-subsumed reachable residuals, and succinct existential summary size.
https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.MFCS.2017.26
https://eccc.weizmann.ac.il/report/2019/178/

There is also an exact cut communication example hiding in the affine calculation. Compress the q=2^λ shared feasible syndromes to symbols. The original relation on valid symbols is equality, with optional all-zero rows or columns from infeasible symbols. For q≥2 the positive overlapping and disjoint rectangle counts are both q by the diagonal fooling set. The negative overlapping count is the smallest t with binom(t,floor(t/2)) ≥ q. To prove it, on valid symbols a zero rectangle has disjoint left and right symbol sets. Enlarge it to A×(symbols\A). For every ordered pair of distinct symbols the left membership code must have a coordinate 1 where the right code is 0. This is exactly the antichain condition. Choose a middle-layer code of length t for the upper bound. Infeasible rows and columns can join all the left and right sets, respectively, because the codewords are nonempty and nontotal. Negative disjoint count is q if at most one side has an infeasible symbol class, and q+1 if both do, over the reals by rank of J−I_q and its padded versions, with row or column classes giving the partitions. The dominant override adds a positive rectangle iff there is an infeasible left class. The negative overlapping count grows only about λ+(log2 λ)/2 while the exact residual count is 2^λ. This affords another small diagram that makes the requested distinction between rank, residuals and rectangle polarity visible.

What would strange week-30 data have to do to matter for P versus NP? An arbitrary finite record can supply a counterexample to a proposed invariant or illustrate a model-specific theorem. The success criterion for a generator deserves an exact quantifier. A uniform formula-aware polynomial-time algorithm that emits a verified satisfying witness with probability at least 1/poly(n) for every satisfiable arbitrary CNF would put SAT in RP: verify and repeat, with no accepting witness on UNSAT. Conversely SAT in RP gives such a sampler via amplified decision-to-search self-reduction, with a polynomially small per-query error. Under a deterministic exact progress guarantee the analogous conclusion is P=NP. For formula-oblivious assignment sampling there is a separate elementary hard case: among unit-clause formulas with each distinct unique assignment, some assignment is hit by K proposed candidates with probability at most K/2^n. That calculation is about an information restriction and says nothing about reading the formula, which makes those instances trivial. The precise boundary is what the generator is allowed to learn from F and the cost of using it universally.

