Write p for the number of tagged continuations (z nodes) and Y for the number of y nodes. Tags have distinct low children, and both the set of low children and the set of untagged continuations have size at most Y+1 including zero. Every x row picks a pair of continuation states with at least one tag. The pair's support union must equal that x row's support. Therefore 512≤p(Y+1)+p(p+1)/2. If p+Y≤35, p≤Y+1 forces the right side ≤495, a contradiction. Thus p+Y≥36.

