If H has a full-PC width-three encoding attaining its own r_H−2 floor with r_H≥2, the new lower bound is exact. Use its encoding E_H(y_H,¬s_H) and the complete multipartite witness encoding E_K(y_K,¬s_K), then impose z∨s_H∨s_K. The first factor is the branch selected only if s_H is true; the second mirrors it. One variable per factor separator makes singleton-overlap PC gluing apply. The groups alone take Σ(|A_j|−2) auxiliaries, the branch selectors add two, and H contributes r_H−2. For ordinary graph H⊔K_(p,q), p,q≥2, the minimum is r_H+p+q−4 for such H. Examples are P6⊔K_(p,q) giving p+q, and an r-edge matching⊔K_(p,q) giving r+p+q−4. The matching upper can use an OR split with each pair as a block term, distribute each local clause to width three, and apply singleton gluing.

