For a maximal minimal cover C of C5, fix the fully false row with z=0, the three blocker vertices inactive, and all other vertices active. Each of z and the three blockers is essential. A refutation needs both auxiliaries: with one the two clauses must both saturate width three to cover four visible slots and two auxiliary slots, yet the z clause is binary. With two the three clauses have exactly one width slot to spare, used by the binary z clause. Its other literal cannot be a visible one, since no visible x is forced on the C5 witness branch. A binary clause of the form z∨a starts the trace; signs can be normalized. If two different bits were both initially forced by binary z clauses, prioritize those units; the remaining falsified clause would leave fewer than eight available slots in the trace. Thus only one bit can be pinned this way. Clause counting forces the other two clauses, up to order, to be (b^σ∨x_i∨x_j) and (¬a∨b^(−σ)∨x_k), splitting the three cover vertices into a pair and a singleton. At z=1 and x all zero the unguarded clause for each cover requires the same b sign in a single legal extension. Choose that sign positive.

