The Chaitin connection is the difference between exhibiting a short description and ruling out all shorter descriptions. The finite map has a named interpreter, grammar and clock, which makes the latter an exhaustive, decidable check within those limits. Changing seeds can expose mistakes in the implementation or the checks. A future scope extension needs a checked enumeration or a proof that reduces the new cases to existing ones. This pilot records its exact scope, seed, commit, checker/implementation hashes and outcome in an Actions artifact. It does not enable a release gate or change the mutation configuration.
