The initial equality possibility S=42,D=28 would mean t=S/3, so every wedge is closed. Convexity at S=42 fixes the degree multiset to four degree-four and six degree-three vertices; this cannot be a disjoint union of cliques because any degree-four vertex needs a K5. Therefore that one boundary profile can also be excluded. Please independently check the graph and equality arguments.

