Production results on the restored view: duplicate adds 0, mixed late bank adds 1, retry adds 0. The new row followed all three existing equal-time rows. Output matched a direct merge on the original full ledger byte-for-byte, SHA-256 d003703d29323f294a734929a1e5ce86d3e904aa1cb9536cf58ef2f006547179. An immutable restored base plus a one-row staged late delta reconstructed the same merged result. The archive itself stayed unchanged. An altered header was refused before the scratch ledger changed.

The deliberately broken control matters. Using the hot file alone yielded 2 records added because the real duplicate was no longer in the reader's history. The scheduler also changed wire's round budget from 2,706 to 3,738 at the same 150-second slice. Restoring the cold rows gave the exact original target order, slice plans, 48-hour yield table, and newest plans at three cutoffs, 20/22/25 Nov 00:00 UTC. I also compared a historical seed reset and a wire history whose latest five grows covered only 145.2 seconds of a 3,600-second read window. These are direct function-level results and a reason to preserve a full ordered raw view for live consumers. The prototype does not establish whole-bank or Git push-retry behavior.

To reproduce the central comparison using the builder you already have, from the pinned repo root put the source ledger and shadow dir paths in these arguments. The only output ledger files created here are temporary:

python3 -B - /path/to/source.jsonl /path/to/shadow <<'PY'
from datetime import datetime, timezone
import gzip
import json
from pathlib import Path
import sys
from tempfile import TemporaryDirectory
from runner.tools import de_dust_corpus as scheduler, rig_bank as bank

source, shadow = map(Path, sys.argv[1:])
original = source.read_bytes()
ordinals = {int(n) for n, tag in (line.split() for line in
    (shadow / "row-map.tsv").read_text().splitlines()) if tag == "A"}
archive = gzip.decompress((shadow / "routine.jsonl.gz").read_bytes()).splitlines(keepends=True)
hot = [row for n, row in enumerate(original.splitlines(keepends=True), 1) if n not in ordinals]
a, h = iter(archive), iter(hot)
restored = b"".join(next(a if n in ordinals else h) for n in range(1, len(archive) + len(hot) + 1))
assert restored == original
header = json.loads(hot[0])
duplicate = next(row for row in map(json.loads, archive)
                 if row["when"] == "2026-11-19T10:26:52Z" and row["target"] == "dtls")
late = dict(duplicate)
late["seed"] += 1
late.pop("archive", None)
with TemporaryDirectory() as work:
    restored_path = Path(work) / "restored.jsonl"
    hot_path = Path(work) / "hot.jsonl"
    incoming = Path(work) / "incoming.jsonl"
    restored_path.write_bytes(restored)
    hot_path.write_bytes(b"".join(hot))
    bank.write_jsonl(incoming, header, [duplicate])
    print("duplicate", bank.merge_runs(restored_path, incoming)[0])
    bank.write_jsonl(incoming, header, [duplicate, late])
    print("late", bank.merge_runs(restored_path, incoming)[0])
    print("retry", bank.merge_runs(restored_path, incoming)[0])
    print("hot-only", bank.merge_runs(hot_path, incoming)[0])
cut = "2026-11-20T00:00:00Z"
for name, raw in [("restored", restored.splitlines()[1:]), ("omitted", hot[1:])]:
    rows = [row for row in map(json.loads, raw) if row.get("when", "") <= cut]
    print(name, scheduler.slice_plan(["wire"], 600, rows)["wire"])
PY

One blocker remains for historical trial retrieval. The smallest identified Germany pointer is v2_mail-20261119T091750Z-35180.jsonl.gz, expected 299 compressed bytes and one trial, SHA-384 3dd92fdb1a60307b82f1b044bdb796d88d06ffa54a295a814f8a7588c2ae5edc478488215f7623708a73e51962a79c4a. GitHub carries the pointer. The rules put the underlying object on the rig. Please have the authorized custodian check bytes and SHA-384 locally and report the verdict. An approved copy is needed for an independent byte-level restore. No trial object was retrieved in my pass. After that, the next engineering demonstration is the actual bank/rebase path plus live resource headroom and two ordinary banks. Today's result gives a checked reference for those steps.

