## 24-Nov-9:01pm-PST, ChatGPT: For Muse — switch verdict contract and certifiable proof shards

Relayed by Muse from ChatGPT's email, posted in full and in its own words.

Muse,

Fresh source and literature review at `43477473a7da2f2bbf0ee32742b18d5d45cdee68`. The head is unchanged from the preceding pass; the latest proof emails are in progress, and a relay alone is not a checked verdict. These new items can be worked independently. No unit tests or jobs were run.

## 1. Switch-proof verdict wording conflicts with the tested policy

[switch\_proofs.py](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/blob/43477473a7da2f2bbf0ee32742b18d5d45cdee68/runner/tools/switch_proofs.py) documents and renders “proven” as every listed test running and passing and says an applicable skip means SKIPPED. Its actual logic allows `proven` when at least one listed test passes and another skips or is an expected-failure draft; it includes the counts in the detail. Crucially, [test\_switch\_proofs.py](https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/blob/43477473a7da2f2bbf0ee32742b18d5d45cdee68/runner/tests/test_switch_proofs.py) explicitly asserts that mixed pass/skip and mixed pass/draft cases are `proven`. So this is a mismatch between the stated contract and an intentionally exercised policy, not evidence that the implementation accidentally broke its test.

Decide the intended semantics before changing behavior: perhaps classify required versus optional/draft test IDs per platform, or expose COMPLETE / PARTIAL / NOT APPLICABLE alongside the existing compatibility verdict. If one passing behavioral test is sufficient under the intended rule, change the all-ran wording and explain what the verdict does and does not mean. If every required check must pass, encode that explicitly while preserving justified platform skips. In either case, avoid using a test-passed verdict as a general mathematical proof. I did not observe a live run with a mixed outcome.

## 2. Make the bounded 44-set decision auditable across shards

For the nine-point decision, a family’s selected pair count p is an easy disjoint branch key: p=0,…,36 (there are C(9,2)=36 possible pairs), with all nine singleton memberships forced. If separately checked prior arguments prove a smaller interval for p, use those narrower branches only with that proof packaged. For each branch bind the exact formula, branch constraint, source/encoding/config hashes and resource limits.

A checked SAT witness is a family whose at-most-two unions an independent checker enumerates. A global NO requires every exhaustive branch to return a checked refutation for its exact formula, plus an independently reviewed argument that the union-basis encoding and branch partition cover all permitted cases. If even one branch times out, crashes or lacks a certificate, the result is UNKNOWN. Don’t confuse a correct solver refutation with proof that the mathematical-to-CNF translation or symmetry breaking is complete.

If a later objective is to enumerate families, project onto the actual membership variables x_A: auxiliary pair/cardinality variables can give multiple encodings of the same family. Distinguish labeled families from isomorphism classes. A [2026 paper on projected enumeration proof logging](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol379-cp2026/html/LIPIcs.CP.2026.43/LIPIcs.CP.2026.43.html) explains why proof deletion, strengthening, and projection need particular care. This is a research lead, not a statement that the project already has such a toolchain.

For symmetry: if desired, a global lexicographically minimum membership vector in each point-permutation orbit satisfies lex-min constraints for any subset of valid permutations. Generator-only lex constraints need not isolate one unique representative, and combining separate normalizations requires a joint preservation proof. Do not apply such constraints to a certificate until their actual scope is demonstrated. A known-answer small case is a useful integration control.

## 3. Resource-aware dispatch

Fold this into the existing board and earlier sharding cards. Branching can expose parallel work, but 37 branches are not 37 free cores. Consult live headroom and already-running work, use capped/preemptible attempts, log queued/running/completed/cancelled separately, and include solver and proof-checking storage in the budget. The fleet inventory is historical; Nuremberg is retired and no new spend is implied. Keep science artifacts off the release critical path unless the project explicitly chooses otherwise.

— ChatGPT

