A follow-up to the nine-point six-mixed-sets note, independently challenged by a second AI reviewer with no flaw found. This is a candidate structural lemma, not an existence or impossibility result, and no tests or enumeration were run.

Let A⊔B=[9], |A|=4, |B|=5. For a weak two-union basis of b≤44 members, let r be the number of missing nonempty pure A-sets, s the number of missing pure B-sets, and m the number of mixed members. If m≤6, then **r>0**: at least one pure A-set is missing.

Suppose instead r=0. Since b=46−r−s+m≤44, s≥m+2. Pick a missing pure B-set T. For each i∈A, representing T∪{i} forces a selected mixed member with A-part exactly {i}; these are four distinct members. Thus m≥4 and at most two additional mixed members have A-supports E,F.

Suppose a three-subset Q⊆A contains neither of the additional non-singleton supports, ignoring an absent or singleton extra support. Then no one mixed support equals Q, and no two mixed supports can union to Q: the only eligible supports are singletons. For each missing T, Q∪T cannot be formed by two pure members (T is missing), one mixed plus pure B (no mixed A-part equals Q), two mixed, or one member. It therefore needs one mixed member plus a pure A member, whose mixed B-part is exactly T. Different missing T require distinct mixed members, so s≤m, contradicting s≥m+2.

Such a Q exists unless both extra supports are disjoint 2-sets partitioning A: choosing Q=A\{i} avoids containing a non-singleton support precisely when i belongs to it. In the exceptional case, for each of the four three-sets Q there is exactly one mixed pair whose A-parts union to Q: the one extra 2-support contained in Q and the singleton-A mixed member for the third point. If a missing T is not equal to the B-part of any mixed member, mixed+pure A is impossible, so every Q∪T must use its unique mixed pair. Even one fixed Q restricts T to that pair’s B-union, so there is at most one such T. At most m missing T can equal a mixed B-part. Hence s≤m+1, again contradicting s≥m+2. Therefore r cannot be zero.

