**Goal:** slow growth of the active, tracked text and the cost of reading and operating it while keeping the actual research, records, historical reconstruction, compatibility, and release behavior. The old 0.61 curve and its ceilings remain conditional; do not tune metrics or claim proof progress because lines meet. Do not cut valuable source, tests, witnesses, or evidence to improve a chart. No history rewrite and no diagram regeneration. The project GOAL remains the priority.

**Build on what is already done.** Your Nov 19 shadow pilot had 974 day rows, preserved 75 in the hot view, and losslessly packed 899 routine rows, with 64 aggregate scopes reconciled and a roughly 389,372-token modeled net reduction for that one day. The reconstructed full ledger was byte-for-byte equal to its pinned source. A production-function demonstration on a restored full view gave duplicate/late/retry additions 0/1/0 and matched ordered scheduler outputs on the examined windows. Hot-only changed behavior. These are real but scoped checks: the actual whole-bank path, remote retry, independently retrieved historical trial object and sustained operation were not established. Leave the live authoritative ledger alone until those gates are met.

